<https://data.open.ac.uk/query> a void:Dataset ;
    dcterms:creator "Dawn Kanter" ;
    dcterms:description """This project helped me to discover how the figure of Chiang Kai-shek has been depicted across a range of visual media and across a number of decades. It helped me to examine how a relatively small range of tropes, symbols and icons have continued to recur in such such depictions, despite a wide variety of authors and creators of such imagery.

Beyond this, however, the project helped me break new ground in exploring entirely new forms of propaganda art in China which have seldom been studied before, including pro-Japanese wartime cartooning in Occupied China, and 'living newspaper' dramas in early communist China. I have already published the results of these in two journals (both in open access format).""" ;
    dcterms:identifier "https://data.open.ac.uk/query" ;
    dcterms:license "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/" ;
    dcterms:subject "cross_domain" ;
    dcterms:title "data.open.ac.uk union of all datasets" ;
